# 209: `return;` with no value yields Nil — `Stmt::Return { value: None, .. }`
# in the frozen §3 AST — and it stops the body, so the statement after it never
# runs. An engine that treated a valueless return as a no-op would print
# `after` here.
--- source
fn early() {
  print "before";
  return;
  print "after";
}
print early();
--- expect
before
nil
